---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/site/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/site/SiteFooter.astro';

// Free guide · keyword PLAYBOOK · v2 (2026-10-17). Source: biblioteca/reels/BSK-REEL-20261015-01_iman_PLAYBOOK_prompts_EN_v2.md
const sheetUrl = 'https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1UFSfNHqEu-yQP9g3cg3fppTzgAkpbhyTdp6hJZ920jI/copy';

const columns = [
  ['lead', 'Name or handle', 'You', 'Sara M.'],
  ['playbook', 'ELLIOTT · RIGOUDIS · FRYER · SEGANTINI · NEEDS_HUMAN', 'Prompt 01', 'ELLIOTT'],
  ['next_step', 'What to do next, max 6 words', 'Prompt 01', 'Offer 2 options'],
  ['status', 'draft · approved · sent · skipped', 'You (prompts write draft)', 'draft'],
  ['source', 'Where they came from', 'You or your automation', 'IG comment: PLAYBOOK'],
  ['last_message', 'Their last message, word for word', 'You or your automation', '"how much is it?"'],
  ['last_touch', 'Date of the last message from either side', 'You or your automation', '2026-10-14'],
  ['draft', 'The message, waiting for your OK', 'Prompt 02 or 03', '…'],
];

const prompts = [
  {
    id: 'router',
    step: 'Step 2',
    title: 'Prompt 01 · the router',
    intro: 'Paste it into your assistant with your lead sheet attached (or the rows pasted below it). It fills playbook and next_step for each row and writes no messages yet.',
    text: `You are my lead router. For each row of my lead sheet, fill the
playbook and next_step columns. Do not write any messages yet.

Read source, last_message and last_touch (and who_wrote_last and
context if they exist). Then ask four questions, in this order.
The first YES wins.

Q1 Price, timing or pushback? They asked about price, terms, timing
   or next steps, or pushed back (too expensive, need to think, need
   to ask my partner, "send me info").                    → ELLIOTT
Q2 Problem or call? They described a problem or goal in their own
   words, or booked / asked for a call.                   → RIGOUDIS
Q3 Engaged only? They interacted with my content (commented a
   keyword, replied to a story, followed and said hi) without
   stating a problem.                                     → FRYER
Q4 Otherwise: no contact yet, or a list / form with no context.
                                                          → SEGANTINI

Staleness rule: if I wrote last and last_touch is 14+ days ago, move
ONE step down: ELLIOTT → RIGOUDIS → FRYER → SEGANTINI.
If a row is ambiguous or you would be guessing, write NEEDS_HUMAN.

next_step: max 6 words, the next thing I should do.

OUTPUT, one line per lead:
lead | playbook | next_step | reason (max 12 words)`,
  },
  {
    id: 'drafter',
    step: 'Step 3',
    title: 'Prompt 02 · the drafter',
    intro: 'Paste it after prompt 01, in the same conversation. One first message per row, in the style of its playbook. Every draft waits for you.',
    text: `Now write ONE first message for each row, in the style of its
playbook column. You never send anything; every draft waits for me.

ELLIOTT (inspired by Andy Elliott's public teaching on closing):
- Short sentences, calm certainty, no hedging words.
- Acknowledge what they said before answering it.
- If there is an objection, isolate it: check it is the only thing in
  the way before you answer it.
- Tie the answer to something THEY said, not a feature list.
- End with a clear choice between two concrete options.
- Never offer a discount unless my context says I allow it.

RIGOUDIS (inspired by Chris Rigoudis' public discovery questions):
- Mirror their problem back in their own words.
- Ask what would change once it is solved ("If this were fixed in
  90 days, what would be different?").
- No pitch yet. Invite a call only if they already asked for one.

FRYER (inspired by Coach Brian Fryer's public DM approach):
- Deliver what was promised first (the PDF, the link), no strings.
- One genuine, easy question about them or their situation.
- No pitch, no link to buy, no calendar link in the first message.
- Sound like a person: their name, plain words.

SEGANTINI (inspired by Giulio Segantini's public permission-based
openers):
- Be honest that it is a cold message.
- One real, specific reason you picked them (a post, a hire, a
  launch). If there is no real reason, write NEEDS_HUMAN instead.
- Ask permission for 30 seconds, then one question about their
  problem.

Rules for every draft:
- Max 60 words. Write in the lead's language.
- No fake urgency. Never invent facts or results. Use only the row
  and my context.
- One question per message, max.
- Never pretend to be any of these coaches or quote them.

OUTPUT, one line per lead:
lead | playbook | draft
Put each draft in the draft column with status = draft.`,
  },
  {
    id: 'calls',
    step: 'Step 4',
    title: 'Prompt 03 · calls',
    intro: "Paste it with ONE call transcript attached. Record only with the other person's consent: in some places it's the law.",
    text: `Read this sales call transcript.

1. Quote the moment their interest went up, and the moment it
   dropped, word for word.
2. List every objection in their exact words.
3. Pick one playbook: price, timing or a decision on the table →
   ELLIOTT. Problem still fuzzy → RIGOUDIS. Neither → NEEDS_HUMAN.
4. Write a follow-up email under 80 words in that style (same style
   rules as prompt 02). Subject line max 5 words.
5. Give me one new row for my sheet:
   lead | playbook | next_step | status=draft | source=call |
   last_message (their last words on the call) | last_touch (call
   date) | draft
6. Don't invent anything that wasn't said on the call. If something
   is missing from the transcript, say so instead of guessing.`,
  },
];

const tools = [
  ['ASSISTANT · REQUIRED', 'Claude, ChatGPT or Gemini', 'I use Claude in the video.', true],
  ['SHEET · REQUIRED', 'Google Sheets', 'For your copy of the lead sheet.', true],
  ['LEADS IN · OPTIONAL', 'ManyChat, Tally or Calendly', 'Or paste them by hand.', false],
  ['CALLS · OPTIONAL', 'Fathom, tl;dv, Otter or Fireflies', 'Free recorders that export transcripts.', false],
];
---

<Layout
  title="PLAYBOOK: 3 prompts and a lead sheet · Mario Perera"
  description="Three prompts that pick the right sales playbook for each lead, draft the message in that style and turn a recorded call into a follow-up. Free guide."
>
  <SiteHeader />
  <main>
    <section class="wrap hero">
      <div class="copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Free guide · keyword PLAYBOOK</p>
        <h1>PLAYBOOK: 3 prompts and a lead sheet</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Three prompts that decide which sales playbook fits each lead, draft the message in that style, and turn a
          recorded call into a follow-up. Nothing gets sent. You read, edit and send.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="btn" href="#prompts">Get the prompts ↓</a>
          <a class="btn ghost" href={sheetUrl} rel="noopener">Copy the lead sheet</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside aria-label="What's inside">
        <div class="row"><span>Copy-paste prompts</span><b class="mono">3</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span>Lead sheet template</span><b class="mono">1</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span>Works with</span><b class="mono">Claude · ChatGPT · Gemini</b></div>
        <p>
          Inspired by what four sales coaches teach in public: Andy Elliott, Chris Rigoudis, Coach Brian Fryer and Giulio
          Segantini. Not affiliated with any of them. If you like a style, buy their training.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="members">
      <div class="wrap members-inner">
        <div class="members-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Members</p>
          <p class="members-title">Skip the copy-paste. Your AI sets this up.</p>
          <p>Connect the vault to Claude or ChatGPT and say: <span class="mono">set up PLAYBOOK for my business</span>.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="btn" href="/welcome">Join the vault</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="prompts" class="wrap steps">
      <article class="step">
        <div class="step-copy">
          <span class="mono label">Step 1</span>
          <h2>The lead sheet</h2>
          <p>One row per lead. The template opens a copy in your own Google Drive; the rows in it are made-up examples.</p>
          <a class="link-arrow" href={sheetUrl} rel="noopener">Copy the sheet →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="table-box">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Column</th><th>What goes in it</th><th>Who fills it</th><th>Example</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {
                columns.map(([col, what, who, ex]) => (
                  <tr>
                    <td class="mono">{col}</td>
                    <td>{what}</td>
                    <td>{who}</td>
                    <td>{ex}</td>
                  </tr>
                ))
              }
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </article>

      {
        prompts.map((p) => (
          <article class="step">
            <div class="step-copy">
              <span class="mono label">{p.step}</span>
              <h2>{p.title}</h2>
              <p>{p.intro}</p>
            </div>
            <div class="prompt">
              <pre id={`prompt-${p.id}`}>{p.text}</pre>
              <div class="prompt-bar">
                <button type="button" class="copy" data-copy={`prompt-${p.id}`}>Copy prompt</button>
                <span class="copied mono" role="status" hidden>Copied</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </section>

    <section class="band">
      <div class="wrap tools">
        <h2>What you'll need</h2>
        <div class="tool-grid">
          {
            tools.map(([kind, name, note, required]) => (
              <div class:list={['tool', { required }]}>
                <span class="mono kind">{kind}</span>
                <strong>{name}</strong>
                <span>{note}</span>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap rules">
      <h2>Before you automate anything</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Instagram gives a business 24 hours to answer after a person writes. Never use automations to message people cold.</li>
        <li>Cold emails and messages have their own rules where you live. In Europe, check GDPR first.</li>
        <li>Tell people you are recording a call. In many places you need their consent.</li>
        <li>The prompts decide which play. The conversation, and the trust, are still yours.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <p class="wrap disclaimer mono">
      v2 · 2026-10-17 · Not affiliated with Andy Elliott, The Elliott Group, Chris Rigoudis, Coach Brian Fryer, Giulio
      Segantini or Underdog Sales.
    </p>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Layout>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('button[data-copy]').forEach((button) => {
    button.addEventListener('click', async () => {
      const pre = document.getElementById(button.dataset.copy ?? '');
      const status = button.parentElement?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.copied');
      if (!pre) return;
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(pre.textContent ?? '');
        if (status) {
          status.hidden = false;
          setTimeout(() => (status.hidden = true), 2000);
        }
      } catch {
        const range = document.createRange();
        range.selectNodeContents(pre);
        const selection = window.getSelection();
        selection?.removeAllRanges();
        selection?.addRange(range);
      }
    });
  });
</script>

<style>
  .hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 420px), 1fr));
    gap: 48px;
    align-items: start;
    padding-top: 64px;
    padding-bottom: 48px;
  }

  .copy {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 20px;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 900;
    font-size: clamp(34px, 4.2vw, 56px);
    line-height: 1.02;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .lede {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 48ch;
    font-size: 20px;
    color: var(--body);
  }

  .actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .btn.ghost {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--ink);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--ink);
  }

  aside {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 8px;
  }

  aside .row {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 16px 24px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  aside p {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 16px 24px;
    background: var(--blue-tint);
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--body);
  }

  .members {
    background: var(--night);
    color: #F5F5F5;
  }

  .members-inner {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 24px;
    padding-top: 40px;
    padding-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .members-copy {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
    flex: 1 1 520px;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .members .eyebrow {
    color: var(--night-muted);
  }

  .members-title {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 900;
    font-size: 26px;
    line-height: 1.1;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .members-copy p {
    margin: 0;
    color: #D4D6DA;
  }

  .members .mono {
    color: #FFFFFF;
  }

  .steps {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 56px;
    padding-top: 64px;
    padding-bottom: 64px;
  }

  .step {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 320px), 1fr));
    gap: 24px 48px;
  }

  .step-copy {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  .label {
    font-size: 13px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .step h2,
  .tools h2,
  .rules h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 900;
    font-size: 28px;
    line-height: 1.08;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .step-copy p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--body);
  }

  .step-copy .link-arrow {
    align-self: flex-start;
  }

  .table-box {
    overflow-x: auto;
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 8px;
  }

  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 15px;
  }

  th {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 12px 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  td {
    padding: 10px 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #ECEDEF;
    vertical-align: top;
  }

  tr:last-child td {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  .prompt {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    min-width: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 8px;
  }

  pre {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 20px;
    max-height: 420px;
    overflow: auto;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13.5px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .prompt-bar {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 10px 12px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    background: #F7F7F8;
  }

  .copy {
    height: 44px;
    padding: 0 16px;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--ink);
    color: #FFFFFF;
    font-family: inherit;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 15px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .copied {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--blue);
  }

  .band {
    background: var(--paper);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .tools {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 24px;
    padding-top: 56px;
    padding-bottom: 56px;
  }

  .tool-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 240px), 1fr));
    gap: 16px;
  }

  .tool {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
    padding-top: 12px;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--rule);
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--body);
  }

  .tool.required {
    border-top-color: var(--ink);
  }

  .tool strong {
    font-size: 17px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .kind {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .rules {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 420px), 1fr));
    gap: 32px;
    padding-top: 56px;
    padding-bottom: 56px;
  }

  .rules ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 20px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
    color: var(--body);
  }

  .disclaimer {
    padding-bottom: 32px;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
</style>
